%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: ToRiverwood 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I never really gave much appreciation to my walks to school.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474705638883538
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I imagine this would suck way more if I didn't walk regularly.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Then again, the hills do make this definetively worse than the walk to
      school.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Also the lack of Sayori. That doesn't help either.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: After a few minutes of walking, I come upon the Guardian Stones.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652608
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: In the game, interacting with them would give you a permanent buff.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: For these three, it would be an increase to experience gained for the
      skills that correspond to Warriors, Mages, and Thieves.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I wonder what they'd do for me?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I walk up next to the Warrior Stone, the one I usually go with.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Standing next to it, I can feel something...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I would say magical, but I feel like that wouldn't be accurate.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I reach out my hand to touch the stone...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: At my touch, the stone lights up, projecting a beacon into the sky.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I feel... something?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: What it did to me, I'm not sure, but I guess it'd be better to have its
      boon than to not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: With archaic rock power flowing through me(?), I continue my journey
      to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: After another few minutes, and a couple encounters with unfriendly fauna,
      I arrive to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652660
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Remember not to hit the chicken!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, time to take stock of my situation.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Foreign land, no money, I have a weapon, but no food.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'Hmm. '
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I suppose there's nothing stopping me from getting help from both Alvor
      and Gerdur...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: If I remember right, Gerdur should have food, Alvor has smithing materials,
      and both should have some gold they can spare me...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'Alright. Step one: get stuff from the town, step two...'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hmm...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I could stick around here and work the mill or something...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... but there'd still be dragons going around.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Assuming of course that they'll be resurrected irregardless of whether
      or not the dragon at the western watchtower is defeated.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Unlike the actual game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... oh crap, is Dawnguard installed?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: That's a weird way of putting it, but I assume that those events are
      canon to the story.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Which this world <i>seems</i> to be following...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I guess I'll warn Balgruuf about the dragons and see where to go from
      there.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright! First, Gerdur.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I make my way to the lumbermill, where Gerdur should be waiting for me.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652661
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hello?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652662
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: Hello stranger, we don't usually get visitors here in Riverwood, what
      brings you here in these troubled times?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Actually, Ralof sent me-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: Ralof? How do you know him?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: He helped me escape from Helgen, and told me to speak with you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: Escape Helgen? What in the world are you talking about?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Did you see a big black thing fly overhead, like, ten minutes ago?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: I- yes. How do you know about that?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That was the dragon that burnt down Helgen, the one Ralof and I helped
      each other escape.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: By the Nine... dragons have returned to Skyrim.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: If there's anyway I can help, just give the word; someone needs to tell
      Jarl Balgruuf about this.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I was planning on heading over there after getting some supplies for
      the journey.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you have any food or septims to spare?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course, any friend of Ralof's is a friend of mine.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Gerdur hands me a bag of septims and a few vegetables.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'm not exactly sure how many septims are in the bag, but I feel like
      it would be faux pas to count the money directly in front of her.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Thanks for the help, I'm heading out for Whiterun now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb230e338deb88646a084896067acdd8, type: 2}
    dialog: Safe travels.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, now to head over to Alvor.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652663
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I make my way to the smithy.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652664
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hey.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652665
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Who are you, stranger?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hadvar told me you'd give me a hand.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Hadvar? How do you know him?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Did you happen to see a big black thing flying overhead around ten minutes
      ago?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: It's rude to answer a question with another question; yes, what about
      it?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That was the dragon that burnt down Helgen, the one Hadvar and I helped
      each other escape.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: A dragon?!? I-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Dark days have come to Skyrim. First the civil war, now dragons have
      returned...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm heading down to warn Jarl Balgruuf about it, after getting some supplies
      for my journey.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you have any septims to spare?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Aye, a friend of Hadvar's is a friend of mine.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alvor hands me a small bag of septims, similar in size and weight to
      Gerdur's bag.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Also, while I'm here, could you help me sharpen my blade?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Interested in smithing, boy?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's see what you're working with here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I draw my weapon, handing it over to Alvor.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, I see... since it's made of iron, this should be easy.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Here, take a seat on the grindstone...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alvor leads me over to the grindstone. I presume I'm about to get a hands-on
      lecture.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652666
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Blade successfully sharpened.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652668
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'm not entirely sure why we had to press the ingot directly onto the
      blade while we were sharpening...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: But I guess that's to justify improving the weapons requiring materials
      in-game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Thanks for the lesson and help, Alvor.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm heading out for Whiterun now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ad912a4f92445545a2225f1d74898be, type: 2}
    dialog: Safe travels.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: With that, I start heading down the road that leads out of town.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652667
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652669
    - rid: 9079475089592287605
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Maybe I'll learn more about how and why I got here if I follow along
      the main quest.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... it'll probably be pretty dangerous, though.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I start my journey toward Whiterun...
    ScreenActions: []
